description: After a successful /verify, commit and push without waiting to be asked.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Post-verify git

When `/verify` (or an equivalent verification pass) succeeds for work that changed the tree:

1. Commit the verified changes with a concise message focused on why.
2. Push to the tracked remote (`-u` when setting upstream).
3. Do not leave a clean verification sitting uncommitted unless the user explicitly said not to push/commit.

Still follow normal git safety: no force-push to main/master, no secrets, no amending others' commits, no skipping hooks.
